Error [E0121]: `pair.left` was consumed by a lambda that captures it, so it can't be used here
  --> moved_places_can_be_reinitialized_without_clearing_relatives_3.jet:8:16
    |
  8 |     print(pair.left)
    |                ^^^^
  --> moved_places_can_be_reinitialized_without_clearing_relatives_3.jet:6:29
    |
  6 |     call(() -> { print(pair.left) })
    |                             ^^^^ `pair.left` moved to a lambda that captures it here
 Why: After a value moves somewhere else, its old name no longer gives access to it
 Fix: Stop using `pair.left` after the move, or give a lambda that captures it a copy with `~pair.left` where it moved.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0121
